  "body": "[The explanation of the insertion mode includes this inaccurate line](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#the-insertion-mode) (bold mine):\n\n> The insertion mode affects how tokens are processed and whether CDATA sections are supported.\n\n[CDATA section handling depends on the adjusted current node](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#markup-declaration-open-state:cdata-section-state), not the insertion mode:\n\n> \"[CDATA[\"\n>   Consume those characters. If there is an adjusted current node and it is not an element in the HTML namespace, then switch to the CDATA section state. Otherwise, this is a cdata-in-html-content parse error. Create a comment token whose data is \"[CDATA[\". Switch to the bogus comment state.\n\n[If CDATA sections are _not_ handled as bogus comments, they emit character tokens.](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#cdata-section-state)\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4016#issuecomment-4913918477.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12658/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 8, 2026, 10:55 AM UTC (5e5fbdb)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12658/74506b6...5e5fbdb/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 8, 2026, 10:55 AM UTC (5e5fbdb)\">diff</a> )",
